Patch: 020-mcp-servers
Reason: an app's remote MCP servers are called by the CLI's own MCP client at the session's model proxy (/mcp/<server>, behind the session key), set over its stdin with setMcpServers (an options.mcpServers entry would be in its argv), each call allowed by name and recorded as a built-in's (intent before it runs, outcome after); a server that does not connect fails the turn, and tool search is off so the granted tools are offered whole
Upstream: ours
Pins: claude-agent: the Claude CLI's own MCP client calls mcp:fake/add through the session's proxy; the fake saw the bearer, the CLI never held it
